   "design": "Members enter online in the gym's member system ({OTHER}), which proposes heats by category and level for the trainer to check; once checked, it sends start times to entrants. On the day scores go into a tablet, the system ranks them for the trainer to check, and checked results are published to the website ({CMS}) and the screen in the gym. Planning and running the competition stay with the trainer.",
   "previous_blocker": "Entries, heats, scores and results were paper and spreadsheets.",
   "enabler_now": "Member systems take event entries; heat and ranking logic is plain code.",
   "still_hard": "Late entries and protests need judgement; scores must be entered right.",
   "human_edge": "Keeping the day fair, fun and on time.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "The trainer checks heats and rankings instead of computing them.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "club volunteer",
     "task": "Run club tournaments",
     "learn": "Whether volunteers can run events with the same tools."
    }
   ],
